  "notes": "{意図|いと} refers to a deliberate, calculated intention behind an action. It often implies a planned or strategic purpose.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {意図|いと}する: to intend, to aim for\n- {意図|いと}が{読|よ}めない: can't read the intention\n- {意図|いと}した{通|とお}りに: as intended\n- {意図|いと}せず: unintentionally\n- {意図|いと}{的|てき}に: intentionally, deliberately\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {意図|いと}: intention, aim (deliberate, calculated, may imply hidden motive)\n- {意向|いこう}: intention, wishes (formal wishes regarding decisions)\n- {目的|もくてき}: purpose, objective (the goal itself)\n- {狙|ねら}い: aim, target (what one is aiming for, slightly informal)",
